      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The Coen Brothers' manic sophomore film Raising Arizona revolutionized comedy with its hyperkinetic visual style and oddball southwestern charm. Following their noir debut <a href=\"/movie/11368\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"11368\">Blood Simple</a> (1984), Joel and Ethan Coen crafted a cartoonish crime caper that pairs Nicolas Cage's ex-con H.I. McDunnough with Holly Hunter's police officer Ed in an unconventional love story about kidnapping a baby. The film's influence appears in later quirky crime comedies like <a href=\"/movie/13685\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"13685\">Bottle Rocket</a> (1996) and <a href=\"/movie/8193\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"8193\">Napoleon Dynamite</a> (2004), while its rapid-fire editing and exaggerated camera movements inspired directors like Edgar Wright and Sam Raimi."
      },
