      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Raising Arizona established the Coens' ability to blend genres seamlessly, combining screwball comedy with crime film elements. This hybrid approach influenced later films like <a href=\"/movie/6415\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"6415\">Three Kings</a> (1999) and <a href=\"/movie/100\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"100\">Lock, Stock and Two Smoking Barrels</a> (1998). The film's unique tone - mixing broad comedy with moments of genuine emotion and surreal violence - created a template for modern indie comedies like <a href=\"/movie/545611\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"545611\">Everything Everywhere All at Once</a> (2022)."
      }
